# ClearHandoff

A complaint-intake and engineering-handoff tool. Customers describe a problem in their own words, answer a few follow-up questions, and get a reference number. Support staff see a structured handoff report, including what is still missing, without having to chase the customer for basics.

**Design principle:** the report never invents facts. The customer's original words are stored exactly as written, and missing details are flagged instead of guessed.

## Features
- Customer complaint form with issue detection and follow-up questions
- Contact details required (email or phone), validated on the server
- Customer tracking page: reference number + contact gives a status, nothing private
- Staff dashboard: tickets, full handoff report, status updates, copy-to-clipboard
- Staff login protecting the dashboard and all ticket data
- 38 automated tests

## Tech
Python, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, SQLite, vanilla JavaScript, pytest

## Run it locally
```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
Set the staff login (PowerShell):
```
$env:STAFF_USERNAME="your-username"
$env:STAFF_PASSWORD="your-strong-password"
```
Start the app:
```
uvicorn main:app --reload
```
- Customers: http://127.0.0.1:8000/
- Tracking: http://127.0.0.1:8000/track
- Staff: http://127.0.0.1:8000/dashboard

## Run the tests
```
pytest
```

## Known limitations (and what I'd build next)
- Issue detection is keyword-based; a model-assisted classifier would handle typos and unusual wording
- Staff login uses one shared credential; next would be per-staff accounts with hashed passwords and a sign-in page
- No email/SMS notifications yet
- SQLite is fine for a prototype; production would use Postgres
- Needs HTTPS before any real deployment